  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🧺 Laundromat Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a laundromat, launderette or laundry service, from Lint Condition Laundry to The Old Wash House."
    },
    "intro": "Name your shop with this **Laundromat Name Generator**: for laundromats and launderettes (or laundrettes, as many UK shops spell it), wash and fold and delivery services, and dry cleaners. Pick a style and your kind of laundry, or add your first name or town.",
    "sections": [],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do I check a laundromat name is free?",
        "answer": "Press Check on any name to see whether it's free as a company, a domain and a social media handle. In the UK, search Companies House; in the US, search your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search. Check your local area too, as two similar names nearby confuse customers."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is a good name for a laundromat?",
        "answer": "A good laundry name is short enough to read on a shop sign from across the street and tells people what you do: \"Laundromat\" or \"Coin Laundry\" in the US, \"Launderette\" in the UK, \"Wash & Fold\" for a service, \"Dry Cleaners\" for pressing. Puns on socks, suds and folding (\"Lint Condition Laundry\") are remembered and shared; a family or street name (\"Hartley's Dry Cleaners\") feels established. Read any pun aloud before you commit: laundry jokes can slide into double meanings, and \"laundering\" means something else entirely."
      }
    ]
  },
